    <title>Binary Kloosterman sums using Stickelberger's theorem and the Gross-Koblitz formula</title>
    <updated>2010-05-28T13:31:43Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1005.4548v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1005.4548v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Let $\mathcal{K}(a)$ denote the Kloosterman sum on the finite field of order $2^n$. We give a simple characterization of $\mathcal{K}(a)$ modulo 16, in terms of the trace of $a$ and one other function. We also give a characterization of $\mathcal{K}(a)$ modulo 64 in terms of a different function, which we call the lifted trace. Our proofs use Fourier analysis, Stickelberger's theorem and the Gross-Koblitz formula.</summary>
